[
 {
  "id": "M21/p1",
  "lesson": "M21",
  "kind": "prediction",
  "prompt": "<p>What is the probability, in percent, that you are ill?</p>",
  "answer": "9",
  "answerKind": "numeric",
  "tol": 1,
  "options": [],
  "explain": "<p>About 9 percent. In 100,000 people, 100 are ill and 99 of them test positive; of the 99,900 healthy, 1 percent, 999, also test positive. So 99 of 1,098 positives are ill: 9.0 percent. The test is accurate, but the healthy outnumber the ill so heavily that its small error rate produces ten false alarms for every true case.</p>"
 },
 {
  "id": "M21/p2",
  "lesson": "M21",
  "kind": "prediction",
  "prompt": "<p>You take a second, independent test, and it is positive again. What now?</p>",
  "answer": "c",
  "answerKind": "choice",
  "tol": 0,
  "options": [
   {
    "key": "a",
    "html": "<p>Still about 9 percent: a second test adds nothing.</p>"
   },
   {
    "key": "b",
    "html": "<p>99 percent: the test's accuracy.</p>"
   },
   {
    "key": "c",
    "html": "<p>About 91 percent: the first posterior becomes the new prior.</p>"
   },
   {
    "key": "d",
    "html": "<p>100 percent.</p>"
   }
  ],
  "explain": "<p>About 91 percent. After the first positive the odds of illness are <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>99</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>999</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">99 : 999</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">99</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">:</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">999</span></span></span></span>; a second positive multiplies them by <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>99</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">99 : 1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">99</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">:</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>, giving <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>9801</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>999</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">9801 : 999</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">9801</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">:</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">999</span></span></span></span>, about <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>91</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">91</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">91</span></span></span></span> percent. This relies on the tests being independent given the disease status; two runs of the same flawed test are not, and the second adds less.</p>"
 },
